 documents.content is one JSON object. Its shape is versioned by indexer_version, so a format change is a new indexer version and new documents; documents are never migrated in place. {
  "version": 12,
  "package_path": "example.org/service/invoices",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "id": "3f9c…64 hex…",
      "key": "v1:[\"method\",\"\",\"example.org/service/invoices\",\"Store\",\"Save\",\"\",\"(context.Context,Invoice)->error\"]",
      "kind": "method",
      "visibility": "exported",
      "shape": "func (s *Store) Save(ctx context.Context, inv Invoice) error",
      "public_shape": "func (s *Store) Save(ctx context.Context, inv Invoice) error",
      "public_hash": "9d2a…64 hex…",
      "private_hash": "51b7…64 hex…",
      "content_hash": "c4e1…64 hex…",
      "name": [12, 17, 12, 21],
      "name_bytes": [418, 422],
      "extent": [12, 1, 30, 2],
      "extent_bytes": [406, 902]
    }
  ],
  "occurrences": [
    { "symbol": "b21e…64 hex…", "role": "call", "range": [15, 9, 15, 13], "bytes": [511, 515], "enclosing": "3f9c…64 hex…" },
    { "symbol": null, "role": "reference", "range": [16, 2, 16, 3], "bytes": [520, 521], "enclosing": "3f9c…64 hex…", "note": "local binding" }
  ],
  "diagnostics": [
    { "range": [40, 1, 40, 20], "message": "undefined: Foo" }
  ]
} symbols lists every symbol the file declares, sorted by extent start: package-level types, functions, methods, variables, and constants, plus the fields and interface methods of the literal struct and interface types they declare. key is the v1 IdentityKey() the syntax extractor already produces, which maps an explorer tree node to its entry and is the only identity a syntax document has (id is null there). name is the identifier range shown in navigation; extent is the whole declaration including its doc comment. A proven type declaration in format v2 has type_form set to struct, interface, other, or alias; the validator checks that it agrees with the canonical shape. The query engine classifies immutable v1 type declarations from their stored shape and reports malformed shapes as errors. Format 6 moved implements out of documents into snapshot implements facts; a format 2–5 document may still carry it, and nothing reads it. embeds stays: it names the types the declaration's own embedded fields spell, by identity, which depends only on the declaration and its direct imports. shape, public_shape, public_hash, private_hash, content_hash, and visibility are the diff inputs; every symbol has shape and content_hash, and a symbol with an id also has public_shape, public_hash, and private_hash. A syntax document renders shape from source text and omits public_shape, public_hash, and private_hash. In a partial document a declaration whose identity or shape involves an invalid type is not proven: it keeps its syntax facts (key, source-rendered shape, content_hash) with a null id and no public_shape, public_hash, private_hash, type_form, or embeds, or is omitted when the syntax extractor has no entry for it. Format 5 replaced format 4's shape_hash and body_hash with the three layers; a database holding format 4 documents is discarded on open (see the cutover).occurrences lists every identifier use in the file, sorted by start byte. role is definition, reference, call, write, type, or import; an embedded field's name is both a definition of the field and a type use of the embedded type, and an import's occurrence spans its path literal and names the imported package's package symbol. symbol is null when the target is not a canonical symbol or could not be resolved; note then states why: local binding (parameters, results, receivers, and function-scoped declarations), type parameter, label, member of a local or anonymous type, unresolved import, unproven: involves an invalid type, or unresolved (the type checker recorded no object). In a syntax document every occurrence is a call with a null symbol and a target field holding the structured identifier the AST extractor records today. In a typed document a call occurrence carries the same call locator, spelled from the type checker: target names the callee's package, receiver type for a method, and name; resolvable is whether symbol is non-null; local_root whether target.package is the document's package; statement_path numbers the calls of the enclosing declaration in byte order; text is the callee expression as written; and enclosing_key is the enclosing declaration's key. A conversion T(x) is a type occurrence, not a call. enclosing is the innermost declared symbol containing the occurrence other than the one a definition occurrence defines, or null at file scope or when that declaration is unproven.excluded, present only on an excluded document, states why the file was not extracted: build constraints exclude the file, or no package builds from its directory, under the recorded GOOS, GOARCH, CGO_ENABLED, and tags. An excluded document has empty symbols and occurrences.diagnostics holds the package's load and type errors positioned in this file, with messages relative to the module root so that a document does not depend on the checkout's location. A syntax document produced because its package failed to load carries them too.Ranges are [start_line, start_utf16_column, end_line, end_utf16_column], one-based; byte spans are [start, end), zero-based. The publisher rejects any range whose end does not follow its start, and any two symbol extents that overlap other than by nesting.Explorer and nodes fields. Until typed documents replace them, each symbol entry also carries the per-declaration data the browse API and nodes queries read, so no second projection exists: identifier (the structured uir.Identifier whose IdentityKey() is key), parent_key (the parent declaration's key, absent for a top-level type), child_slot (types, fields, or methods), ordinal (the declaration's extraction order), payload (the UIR node JSON), semantic_hash (the node's Hash()), and, for struct fields, field (the field projection). A typed document takes these fields from the AST extraction of the same bytes, matched by name span. A declaration the AST extractor does not project (a variable, a constant, an interface method, or a field of a nested literal struct) carries an identifier built from its owner chain, so key still maps it, but no child_slot, payload, or semantic_hash; browse and nodes list only entries with a child_slot, and the call graph reads only occurrences that carry a call locator. A syntax occurrence also carries enclosing_key (the enclosing declaration's key, since enclosing is null), resolvable and local_root (whether the AST resolved the call's package and whether it names the file's own package), statement_path (calls/NNNNNN in call order within the enclosing function), and text (the callee expression as written). A syntax symbol's shape is the declaration's source text formatted without comments and body, and its content_hash digests the extent's go/scanner tokens normalized as the content layer describes, resolving the names a declaration binds by block scoping over the syntax tree; a typed document resolves them from the type checker and leaves the same composite literal keys alone, so both give one declaration the same content_hash. package_path is the extractor's package, which carries a _test suffix for an external test package; documents.package_path is the source revision's package. The browse API and nodes matches report a declaration's line and column from the start of name, and end_line from the end of extent. The posting table collapses document roles into integer codes: 0 definition from symbols, 1 reference from every occurrence with a non-null symbol regardless of document role, and 3 embeds from each embeds entry (storage.PostingRole); code 2 implements exists only in the postings of format 2–5 documents. A posting row names its document by ordinal and its symbol by handle; the primary key (document_ordinal, symbol_handle, role) serves the per-document probe and the document cascade, and symbol_postings_symbol_idx (symbol_handle, role, root_ordinal, document_ordinal) serves the per-symbol range, so a lookup filtered to one root never reads other roots' postings. Builtins receive no postings; their fan-in is useless for navigation and dominates row counts. The publisher verifies before writing that every posting's symbol appears in the document, that every symbol a new document needs has a handle consistent with its module, package, visibility, and kind, that symbol_count and occurrence_count equal the document's array lengths, that every symbol and enclosing value is a known symbol id, that each entry's visibility and kind equal the symbols row, and that package_path equals the source revision's package path. Documents and postings are content-addressed, so a concurrent or repeated publication inserts them with ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING and re-reads, as indexer/modules_sources.go does for source revisions; postings for an existing document are skipped, not duplicated.

